{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "d0e2cef1-9ea2-896b-8908-11b06a17c6a6",
  "created_at": "2026-03-12T11:28:34-04:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Leo Cardillo",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Anita Chaudhry",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:24:48-04:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Anita. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:24:53-04:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yeah, good morning. Um, I'm looking to put up a fence in the back of my yard and I'm not totally sure how this works. Do I need a permit for that?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:25:07-04:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good question. Generally a fence does need a permit here, but it depends on a couple of things. Can you tell me what you're planning? Height, material, where it's going?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:25:20-04:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so, it's along the back property line. I want a six-foot fence. Wicked simple, just across the back. And I was gonna do chain-link, five feet tall."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:25:32-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hold on, so is that six feet or five feet? You said both."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:25:38-04:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh. Yeah, sorry. Um, I want it six, that's what I've been thinking, but the chain-link the guy showed me is the five-foot roll. So I guess I'm planning five? I don't know, is that gonna matter?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:25:53-04:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It can matter, because height is often what changes the rules, especially in a back or side yard. So let's write down five-foot chain-link for now and we'll see if you want to go taller. Are you hiring a contractor or doing it yourself?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:26:11-04:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A contractor. So does he pull the permit, or is that on me, being the owner? I thought maybe he does it but then my brother-in-law said it's the owner. Totally confused now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:26:25-04:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Either can work. Often the contractor applies on your behalf, but the property owner is still responsible for making sure it's done. So ask him straight out whether the permit is in his quote. If he says no, you'd apply yourself."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:26:42-04:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So ask him if it's in the quote. Got it. And what about the neighbor? Do I gotta tell the guy behind me? Like notify him or get him to sign something?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:26:56-04:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'd say it's a good idea to let them know, just as a courtesy. As for whether it's required on the application, I'd want to check that with the zoning officer, because it can depend on where the line sits. Do you know if the fence goes right on the line or a little inside it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:27:19-04:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Uh, right on it, I think? Or maybe a foot in. I'd have to look at the survey. Is that bad?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:27:28-04:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not bad, but it's something you'll want to know before applying. If you can find the survey or plot plan, bring it or send a copy with the application. Do you want me to have someone call you back about the neighbor part?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:27:46-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, that'd be good. My number is 401-555-0195."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:27:50-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, 401-555-0195, and that's Mr...?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:27:53-04:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Cardillo. Leo Cardillo. C-A-R-D-I-L-L-O."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:27:55-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thanks, Mr. Cardillo. I'll note five-foot chain-link, back line, possibly six, and your question on neighbor notice. Someone will get back to you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:28:05-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great. Sorry, I gotta run, actually. My kid forgot his lunchbox and I'm heading over to the school with it right now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:28:15-04:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, go, go. Before you do, just remember to ask the contractor about the permit, and look for that survey."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:28:24-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, the quote and the survey. Okay. I think I got it. Mostly. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T11:28:31-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome. Have a good day."
    }
  ],
